  "body": "The non-normative [index of elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/indices.html#elements-3) currently has `flow*` under \"Categories\" and \"Parents\". Unless I'm missing something, both of these have been incorrect since @domenic removed the `scoped` attribute in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1226. I guess that he missed this because he implemented the removal by reverting 29cf39d2163cfc85b67409f4e10390619ffb2b40 and related commits, but the elements index was not added until 3 years after `scoped` was added (778068cf) and so just looking at the commits that added `scoped` could never reveal this bug.\n\nThe current draft of the W3C's HTML 5.2 spec is similarly affected, despite them having [removed `scoped` independently](https://github.com/w3c/html/pull/318).\n\nIn the next few minutes I'm going to push up a PR to fix this on this repo, open an issue about this on the W3C repo linking to this one, and open a duplicate PR on their repo.\n\n<sub>Aside: the duplication of labour y'all have going on between the two specs is a tragic waste of good people's time and makes me sad.</sub>\n",
